        "original_id": "40f39e1e-8f7c-5775-829b-a0868fef65dd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Pavel Sergeyevich Alexandrov, Gregori Aleksandrovich Margulis\n- Roles: Soviet mathematician, Russian-American mathematician\n- Concepts: lattices in Lie groups, ergodic theory, diophantine approximation\n\nFacts:\n- Pavel Sergeyevich Alexandrov, sometimes romanized as Paul Alexandroff or Aleksandrov, was born on 7 May 1896.\n- Pavel Sergeyevich Alexandrov was a Soviet mathematician.\n- Gregori Aleksandrovich Margulis was born on February 24, 1946.\n- Gregori Aleksandrovich Margulis is a Russian-American mathematician.\n- Gregori Aleksandrovich Margulis is known for his work on lattices in Lie groups.\n- Gregori Aleksandrovich Margulis introduced methods from ergodic theory into diophantine approximation.\n- Pavel Sergeyevich Alexandrov died on 16 November 1982.",
